> On Friday, November 9, 2012 11:00:08 AM UTC-5, Jeffrey Horner wrote:
>
> > Unfortunately, no.
>
> > Shiny represents a new class of web applications that require very little
> > HTTP and a lot of websockets. Whereas traditional web applications,
> > including those hosted on rApache  and Rook, rely on the URL namespace for
> > application logic, location of assets, etc... Shiny applications and those
> > like them house their logic in javascript MVC patterns and communicate
> > solely over websockets.
>
> > Shiny apps are hosted using the R websockets package which acts more like
> > a tcp server than a web server, and that architecture just doesn't fit with
> > rApache, or even apache for that matter.
>
> > Jeff
